# 🛡️ Stay Safe Online — Checklist for College Students (India)

Use this practical checklist to protect your data, money, and privacy online:

## 🔐 Account & Password Safety
- [ ] Use **strong, unique passwords** for every account (at least 12 characters with letters, numbers, symbols).
- [ ] Enable **Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)** on email, social media, and banking apps.
- [ ] Avoid saving passwords on shared/public computers.

## 📱 Device & App Security
- [ ] Install apps **only from official stores** (Google Play Store / Apple App Store).
- [ ] Regularly **update your phone, laptop, and apps** to patch security vulnerabilities.
- [ ] Use a **screen lock (PIN/biometric)** on all devices.

## 🌐 Safe Browsing & Social Media
- [ ] Do not click on **unknown links** in emails, SMS, or DMs (even if they look urgent or from friends).
- [ ] Review and limit what you share publicly—avoid posting **phone number, address, college ID, or travel plans**.
- [ ] Verify job/internship offers—watch for **fake recruiters** asking for fees or personal data.

## 💸 Financial & UPI Safety (Important)
- [ ] **Never share UPI PIN, OTP, or bank details** with anyone—even if they claim to be from the bank or police.
- [ ] Remember: **Receiving money does NOT require entering your UPI PIN**—PIN is only for sending money.
- [ ] Double-check **UPI IDs/QR codes** before paying; scammers often use similar-looking IDs.
- [ ] Avoid using public Wi-Fi for **banking or payments**.

## 🎓 College-Specific Risks
- [ ] Be cautious of **fake scholarship links, exam portals, or fee payment pages**.
- [ ] Don’t download pirated study materials—they may contain **malware/spyware**.

## 🚨 If Something Goes Wrong
- [ ] Immediately report fraud at the **National Cyber Crime Portal**: https://cybercrime.gov.in  
- [ ] Call the **Cyber Crime Helpline: 1930** (for urgent financial fraud).
- [ ] Inform your bank/app provider quickly to try blocking transactions.

---

## ✅ Quick Reminder
> Think before you click, verify before you trust, and act fast if something feels wrong.
